Wow, thanks for the list!  That's everything that could be listed in
final attributes?  I could have sworn I've seen "you were a
werejackal" before, on death.  Oh, well.  It looks like maximizing
final attributes means ascending while polymorphed, and I assume you
can't be polymorphed and a lycanthrope (unless polymorphed into a
werejackal, maybe).

So anyway, I'm going to group these to try to make this little brain
teaser easier...  (I've also done some editing to take into account
other comments.)

Attributes that will always appear:
* You were [aligned].
* You could (not) safely pray.
* You survived (after being killed n times).

Standard attributes that are trivial to obtain and keep:
* You were [crowned].
* You were fire resistant.
* You were cold resistant.
* You were sleep resistant.
* You were disintegration-resistant.
* You were shock resistant.
* You were poison resistant.
* You saw invislble.
* You were telepathic.
* You were (in)visible (to others).  (When does visible get listed?)
* You aggravated monsters.
* You could teleport.
* You had teleport control.
* You were (ineffectively) protected.
* You were (very) fast.
* You were [lucky].
* You had [extra/reduced] luck.
* Good luck did not time out for you.
* Bad luck did not time out for you.

These "ring attributes" are available only from rings.  These will be
limited to 2, plus whatever can be eaten:
* You hungered rapidly.
* You were (poorly) adorned.  (worn only, or stay polymorphed as
  creature that ate it)
* You had a [bonus/penalty] to hit.
* You had a damage [bonus/penalty].
* You had slower digestion.  (worn only)
* You were protected from shape changers.
* You were polymorphing.
* You had polymorph control.
* You had free action.  (worn only)
* You had fixed abilities.  (worn only)

These "ring attributes" can also be obtained by other means.  I also
listed monster-specific warning here.  But how do you get demon/undead
warning, and can you have orc/demon/undead warning and regular warning
at the same time?
* You were warned.  (or from being CHMPW, or carrying (OoF or (MKoT)
* You were aware of the presence of [orcs/demons].  (Wield Sting/?)
* You were warned of undead.  (?)
* You had automatic searching.  (or be AMRaRoT or wield Excal)
* You were stealthy.  (or from cloak, boots, *HoA, prayer, or being
  ABMRaRoSV)
* You caused conflict.  (or from #invoking Sceptre of Might)
* You regenerated.  (or by polymorph, or wielding )SoA)

These attributes are not difficult to acquire, but require some
degree of management since they time out:
* You could recognise detrimental food.  (scroll or spell)
* You [resisted hallucinations / were hallucinating].  (potion is
  easiest)
* You were stunned.  (forgotten spell is easiest)
* You were confused.  (forgotten spell is easiest)
* You had slippery [hands].  (tin; can of grease?)
* You were sensing the presence of monsters.  (potion or spell)
* You were going to confuse monsters.  (scroll or spell)
* You had wounded legs.  (xan attack, bear trap, land mine, kick...)

After the above categories, the attributes get tough to divide up.
A lot of them have multiple ways to obtain them.  Others would only
logically fall into small groups, or groups of just one.  So for now
at least, I'm going to lump the rest into "other attributes":
* You were level-drain resistant.  (wield Excalibur, Stormy, )SoA, or
  polymorph)
* You were magic-protected.  (wear GDSM or CoMR, poly into gray
  dragon, or have one of a number of artifacts)
* You were acid resistant.  (wear Apron or YDSM, or poly)
* You were [petrification resistant / turning to stone].  (poly/c hiss)
* You were blinded.  (blindfold is easiest)
* You were sick from food poisoning.  (old corpse)
* You were sick from illness.  (Pesty attack)
* You were turning into slime.  (slime attack)
* You were being strangled.  (wear amulet; do you get this if you ate
  the amulet as a xorn?)
* You fumbled.  (gauntlets or boots)
* You fell asleep.  (amulet)
* You were clairvoyant.  (cornuthaum, donation to priest)
* You had infravision.  (be dwarf, elf, gnome, orc, or polymorph)
* You were displaced.  (cloak; can you be invisible at same time?)
* You could jump.  (knight, boots, or spell)
* You [were levitating / could fly].  (boots, potion, spell, *HoA,
poly)
* You could walk on water.  (boots)
* You could swim.  (polymorph)
* You could [survive without air / breathe water].  (poly, amulet)
* You could walk through walls.  (poly into X or earth E)
* You were riding [a monster].  (duh)
* You were [holding / held by] [a monster].  (duh)
* You were polymorphed into [a monster].  (duh)
* You could not change from your current form.  (wear amulet)
* You had reflection.  (SDSM, shield, or wield )LoD)
* Your life would have been saved.  (wear amulet)
* You were wielding two weapons at once.  (#twoweapon)
* [Deity] was (very) angry with you.  (piss off your god)

My initial reaction is that a wizard would be best-suited.  You'd
probably want to polymorph a lot of rings and amulets to get the
effects of eating as many as possible.  A lot of attributes can be
caused by spells as well, so general spellcasting would be very
useful.  A monk may also work well, as they can get to at least basic
skill in all spells, and gain attributes with XLs.

It also looks like you'd want to carefully choose a couple artifacts
to burn wishes on, after determining which rings can be eaten.  Armor
will have to be carefully chosen.  And you'd certainly want to ascend
polymorphed - xorn looks like a good candidate, or perhaps a vampire.
And the end game will have to be managed carefully to make sure spells
don't run out, and you don't die and stuff.

This is sounding like a fun stupid ascension trick.  With a little
planning, one should be able to at least get to where you have a third
page of attributes listed at the end.  I'll have to look at this
closer and see what I can do with this.  Any other comments would be
appreciated.  If anyone else tries this first, make sure to YAAP...



